<section class="help-section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="h-faq">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p class="help-section__description">Having problems when searching for items across the cultural collections? Here are some frequently asked questions to help.</p>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">How do I search across multiple collections at once?</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">By default, searches run across every collection in Cultural Collections Search. Use the filters on the results page to narrow a single collection, or to further refine your results by object type, access condition, or date.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">What collections are currently included?</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">The platform is continuously being improved to include items from across the University's museums, archives, art, and scientific collections. Use Browse Collections to see the contributing collections. Please revisit frequently to discover new added items and collections.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Can I download images from my search results?</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">It depends on the item's copyright and terms of use. If a download icon appears near the preview window, you know the image, audio, or video can be used non-commercially. Respectful of the terms of use by always attributing the creator and the University of Melbourne.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">How do I request digital access to a collection item?</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Contact the Collection Team for digital access. It makes the process easier if you include the item's persistent identifier and a description of your intended use.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">How do I report any incorrect or incomplete metadata?</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">We welcome community knowledge to help improve the accuracy of our records. Contact the Collection Team and include the item's persistent identifier to make the process easier.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">What can I do if I have problems accessing the search?</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Try clearing your cache in the browser you are using. Browsers often save outdated information, which is the most common cause of access errors. Here is more information on how to clear your cache on PC or Mac.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">What can I do when there is a broken link on the website</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">If you come across a link that is not working or has taken you somewhere unexpected, retrace your steps from the homepage.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">When all else fails …</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Contact us. To help us fix your problem as quickly as possible, describe the exact steps you took to get the error, and remember, screenshots are worth a thousand words.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="copyright" aria-labelledby="h-copyright">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-copyright">Copyright and Terms of Use</h2>
    <p class="help-section__description">How a collection item can be used varies depending on the conditions of its copyright license, intellectual property or cultural advice. Please check the License type and Terms of Use on individual record for further information.</p>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Free Access</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Collection items available to download may be reused for personal, research, educational or non-commercial purposes. Attribution to the creator and acknowledgement of University of Melbourne is requested.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Licensed</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Some collection items are available for use under Creative Commons or other licence types. Please follow the specific licence terms shown on the individual record.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Cultural Conditions</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Where collection items carrying a cultural or advisory notice, engage respectfully with the content. For more information see <a class="help-copyright__item-link-indigenous-cultural-data" href="<%= indigenous_data_path %>">Indigenous Cultural Data and Access</a>.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Contact the Collection</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Contact the Collection when copyright terms are unclear, or when seeking permission to use collection items in publications, online, and commercial use. To assist in the query, note the information in Cite this item and prepare a description of your intended use.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">University Copyright Office</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">To learn more about copyright and licensing, see the University Copyright Office website, including information on:</p>
      <ul class="help-section__list">
        <li class="help-section__list-item">Basic principles of copyright</li>
        <li class="help-section__list-item">Understanding publishing agreements</li>
        <li class="help-section__list-item">Licences and contracts</li>
        <li class="help-section__list-item">Protecting your work</li>
        <li class="help-section__list-item">Using copyright material</li>
        <li class="help-section__list-item">Copyright and research</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="access" aria-labelledby="h-access">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-access">Access and Information</h2>
    <p class="help-section__description">Do you need to request access or further information on a collection item? Do you want to access and use an image, audio or video?</p>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Contact the relevant collection</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">Contact the relevant collection and include the information from Cite this Item.</p>
      <ul class="help-section__contacts">
        <li class="help-section__contact">
          <span class="help-section__contact-name">Harry Brookes Allen Museum of Anatomy and Pathology (HBA)<br>Henry Forman Atkinson Dental Museum (HFA)<br>Medical History Museum (MHM)</span>
          <span class="help-section__contact-detail">Email: <a href="mailto:MDHS-museum@unimelb.edu.au">MDHS-museum@unimelb.edu.au</a></span>
        </li>
        <li class="help-section__contact">
          <span class="help-section__contact-name">Grainger Museum Collection (GMC)<br>University Art Collection (UAC)</span>
          <span class="help-section__contact-detail">Request Form: <a href="#">Open form</a></span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Response times</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">We will aim to respond to your enquiries within 5 business days. Please note, more complex requests may take additional time.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Feedback</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">We also welcome feedback on how to improve our user experience.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="help-section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="h-privacy">
  <header class="help-section__header">
    <h2 class="help-section__heading" id="h-privacy">Privacy</h2>
    <p class="help-section__description">The University respects the privacy of anyone who interacts with us and is committed to protecting and managing personal and health information fairly and lawfully.</p>
  </header>
  <ul class="help-section__items">
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">Privacy laws</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">University of Melbourne (University) is governed by the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014 (Vic) and Health Records Act 2000 (Vic) (together, Privacy Laws). The University is also considered to be a data controller for the purposes of the EU General Data Protection Regulation 2016/679 (GDPR) in relation to the collection of personal information from individuals located in the EU.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="help-section__item">
      <h3 class="help-section__subheading">How we handle personal information</h3>
      <p class="help-section__text">The University is committed to protecting your privacy and processing your personal information fairly and lawfully in compliance with the Privacy Laws and the GDPR, as applicable. Please refer to our <a class="help-privacy__text-link-privacy-policy" href="https://policy.unimelb.edu.au/MPF1104/">Privacy Policy</a> and our <a class="help-privacy__text-link-privacy-webpage" href="https://about.unimelb.edu.au/strategy/governance/compliance-obligations/privacy">Privacy webpage</a> for information about how we handle personal information.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
